    "elevationMode": "terrain-contact",
    "notes": "One inspected elevated picture supports the curved concrete deck, red/white utility pylons, sagging power lines and narrow river crossing. Standard viewer PMTiles identifies the southern Jamuna Multi-purpose Bridge/N405, separate from the northern railway crossing. Retain original circle/1.75m offset,4800m main spans and128m approaches at each end; mapped centerline5067.95m is slightly longer than5056m source. Approximate east road20.05875m givesbase7.658751514798725m against endpoint model12.4m; west road20.36192m differs0.30m. River preview7.7589m is a coarse mapped-sample surface. Published+11mPWD source zero is not treated as an absolute PMTiles altitude. Exact flood stage, per-pier ground and current former-rail strip conversion remain unverified; retain the authored bare strip. Narrow curved ground opening removes coarse bridge/approach terrain imprint in live placement. The50m-grid preview uses a wider35m contact corridor blended back to raw surroundings by120m; original raw samples remain retained. This is a visualization correction, not river bathymetry or an excavated terrain claim.",
